1.1.text:
Article 3

(1) The purpose of organizing protection for women and children victims of violence is to:

a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect, provide a sense of security for women and children; d. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses;
e. facilitate and mediate household disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.
(2) Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of: a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic neglect;
e. restriction of movement.

Article 13

The Minimum Service Standards as referred to in Article 12 have performance indicators including:

a. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive complaint handling, health services, social rehabilitation services, spiritual guidance services conducted by trained officers within the integrated service unit;
b. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of violence against women and children;
c. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive legal aid services;
d. coverage of repatriation services for women and children victims of violence; and
e. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children victims of violence.

Article 6

(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to provide protection to women and children victims of violence.

(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the regional government as referred to in Article 5 letter a include:

a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children victims of violence based on laws and regulations;
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children victims of violence;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence;
d. facilitating assistance, legal aid and legal services according to the needs of victims;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from victims of violence according to regional financial capacity; and;
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence.
(3) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in a Regional Action Plan as a basis for Regional Apparatus Organizations in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(4) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (3), is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).

Article 9

(1) To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the regional government conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government undertakes the following efforts:

a. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income improvement and social services;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and awareness towards the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; and
g. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Article 10

(1) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 9, is carried out by Regional Apparatus Organizations whose duties and functions are in the fields of:

a. health;
b. education;
c. social;
d. women's empowerment and child protection;
e. peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus Organizations as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and continuous manner based on the regional action plan.

Article 11

(1) In terms of providing protection to women and children victims of violence, the regional government may establish an Integrated Service Center (PPT).

jdih.pakpakbharatkab.go.id

(2) The establishment and development of the PPT is adjusted to the development of priority needs, and the regional financial capacity as well as the institutional capacity of personnel available in the region.

(3) The PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) may accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as P2TP2A, Safe Houses, Child Social Protection Houses, Trauma Center Houses, Women's Social Protection Houses, Shelters and other service activities in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.

(4) Forms of services implemented by the PPT, include:

a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal aid;
e. repatriation;
f. social reintegration.
(5) In providing protection to women and children victims of violence, the PPT is obligated to:
a. provide services as quickly as possible and free of charge to victims; b. organize protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal aid;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and accompanying volunteers needed for victims; d. network with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperate with witness and victim protection institutions, social protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community or other institutions for the health recovery of victims;
e. provide ease, comfort, and safety for victims; f. maintain confidentiality of victims;
g. provide fulfillment of legal aid for victims;
h. in the event that integrated service delivery is carried out through networking, the PPT remains responsible for the entire referral process for services needed by victims.
(6) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (3) is carried out in accordance with Minimum Service Standards.

Article 2

Protection of women and children victims of violence is organized based on the principles of:

a. respect for human rights;
b. gender equality and justice;
c. non-discriminatory;
d. protection of victims' rights;
e. legal certainty.

Article 12

Minimum Service Standards in the field of integrated services for women and children victims of violence, include services for:

a. handling complaints/reports of victims of violence against women and children;
b. health services for women and children victims of violence; c. social rehabilitation for women and children victims of violence; d. law enforcement and legal aid for women and children victims of violence;
e. repatriation and social reintegration for women and children victims of violence. jdih.pakpakbharatkab.go.id

Article 5

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to women and children victims of violence are the shared responsibility of: a. regional government;

b. society;

c. family;

d. parents.

Article 4

Every woman and child victim of violence has the right to receive: a. to have their dignity and honor as human beings respected;

b. protection from family, society, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;

c. health services according to medical needs;

d. special handling related to victim confidentiality; e. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

f. spiritual guidance services;

g. determine their own decisions. jdih.pakpakbharatkab.go.id

