(4) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (3), is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).

Article 3

(1) The purpose of organizing protection for women and children victims of violence is to:

a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect, provide a sense of security for women and children; d. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses;
e. facilitate and mediate household disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.
(2) Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of: a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic neglect;
e. restriction of movement.

Article 9

(1) To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the regional government conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government undertakes the following efforts:

a. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income improvement and social services;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and awareness towards the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; and
g. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Article 13

The Minimum Service Standards as referred to in Article 12 have performance indicators including:

a. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive complaint handling, health services, social rehabilitation services, spiritual guidance services conducted by trained officers within the integrated service unit;
b. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of violence against women and children;
c. coverage of women and children victims of violence who receive legal aid services;
d. coverage of repatriation services for women and children victims of violence; and
e. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children victims of violence.

Article 4

Every woman and child victim of violence has the right to receive: a. to have their dignity and honor as human beings respected;

b. protection from family, society, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;

c. health services according to medical needs;

d. special handling related to victim confidentiality; e. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

f. spiritual guidance services;

g. determine their own decisions. jdih.pakpakbharatkab.go.id

